  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Inter-European Squadron Officer School</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This course is a modified version of the program taught at the USAF Squadron Officer School at Maxwell AFB, which prepares junior officers for increased leadership responsibilities and is their next step on the Professional Military Education (PME) ladder. The curriculum is developed by the Squadron Officer College under USAF Air University guidelines, with minor adjustments for region and culture. Experiential course activities challenge each student to apply curriculum concepts successfully and to influence group dynamics, cohesion, and effectiveness in a positive manner. Graduates are equipped to better lead and motivate personnel, having practiced a variety of leadership, communication, problem-solving, critical thinking, teambuilding and mentoring techniques. IESOS is built around the following blocks of instruction: profession of arms, warfare, leadership, communication, and international security studies. By virtue of its international student body, IESOS fosters positive relationships with other NATO and PfP members, expanding students cultural knowledge in a manner consistent with U.S. and NATO objectives. This course is delivered in parallel with the Inter-European Noncommissioned Officer Academy course to highlight the benefit of a professional officer and NCO corps relationship and develop an understanding of the importance of delegating authority and responsibility for operationally effective high-tempo aviation operations and support.</narrative>
  </description>
